Initial PR regression gates (.github/workflows/regression.yml), from the repository root:

    npm run test:core
    npm ci
    npx playwright install chromium
    npm run test:smoke

The core gate covers the solver, netlist, JS runner, compile status, storage wrapper, account adoption, project save/navigation lifecycle, new-project entry points and sign-in UI contracts. Browser smoke uses a local static server with mocked API/WebSocket traffic; non-local requests are blocked. It covers phone/desktop fast-switch persistence, save failures and retry, header/define retention, Tab copy-on-edit, storage-full Export, and sign-in-off parity. CI uses bundled Chromium. Locally Chrome is the default; PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chromium selects the installed Playwright browser. On Windows, set PLAYWRIGHT_PYTHON="py -3.13" (and use npm.cmd) rather than changing execution policy or a Windows Store Python alias.

Backend contract checks require Linux (or WSL), not native Windows:

    python3 -m venv .venv
    .venv/bin/python -m pip install -r web/tests/requirements.txt
    cd web
    ../.venv/bin/python -m unittest tests.health_route_test tests.auth_test -v

Use an environment outside the checkout or ignore it locally. The dependency file pins the direct test dependencies for Python 3.10 or newer; the backend CI gate uses the locally verified Linux Python 3.10 combination. Backend checks use local provider stand-ins and temporary data; CI explicitly isolates SIM_PROJECT_DIR/SIM_BUILD_DIR and disables warm-up. The broader compile_guard_test suite is not in this initial gate: a Linux run without the compiler, patched QEMU or bwrap had 7 failures, 2 errors and 15 skips, including infrastructure-dependent expectations and QEMU/probe mock mismatches. Investigate these in the supported-toolchain setup work before making them required. A green mocked gate is not a real firmware/sandbox certification.

The full Node suite is NOT gated yet. At the pre-change 6a842e9 baseline it ran 342 tests: 305 passed, 33 failed and 4 skipped. Failures included stale compile/theme and historical schematic fixture assertions, compile-hint expectations, a palette fake-DOM gap, and a Linux-only Chrome launcher on Windows. The core selection is explicit, not a claim that these failures were fixed or that the wider suite passes. Run all web/tests/*.test.js when expanding coverage; bring each failing area into the gate after investigating its baseline failures.

Real toolchain smoke (separate from the mocked PR gates):

Fresh sandboxed compile (real bwrap, real esp-x32 toolchain, same path as /api/compile), then a fresh Blink whose returned id is opened on /api/run and must toggle GPIO2. Skips only when bwrap, the toolchain, or the patched QEMU is missing; SIM_REQUIRE_TOOLCHAIN_TEST=1 makes a missing piece a failure:

    cd web && SIM_REQUIRE_TOOLCHAIN_TEST=1 python3 -m unittest tests.sandbox_toolchain_test -v

The Blink watch is `SIM_TOOLCHAIN_RUN_DEADLINE` seconds (default 15, never above 120). GPIO2 must still toggle at least twice. When it does not, the failure text includes the last 20 UART lines and the gpio and fsel payloads the run saw.
